# apps/indexer — environment variable NAMES only. Copy to apps/indexer/.env.local and fill in.
# THE FILE NAME IS `.env.local`, NOT `.env`.
# Ponder loads `.env.local` from this folder. A file called `.env` here is IGNORED, and the app
# then fails while reading its config, before the HTTP server starts.
# Note that `apps/api` is the other way round: it reads `.env`. Two apps, two file names.
# `.env.local` is gitignored. Never put a real value in this file.

# The RPC for the chain named in packages/chains. The registry holds the NAME of this variable,
# never the URL. Use the public endpoint, https://rpc.testnet.chain.robinhood.com. NOT a keyed
# provider: the indexer fetches every block, about 500,000 calls a day, and burned the Alchemy
# monthly quota. The indexer reads no fallback variable.
ROBINHOOD_TESTNET_RPC_URL=

# The three below are optional and commented out ON PURPOSE. An empty line such as
# `DROPCHAD_CHAIN=` is NOT unset: it sets an empty string, the default is skipped, and the
# indexer crashes at start looking up chain "". The zero from `CONFIRMATION_DEPTH=` would not
# crash but would mark rows `final` at once. That crash loop happened on the server.
# Since then `src/env.ts` reads an empty line as not set, but still: uncomment a line only to give
# it a real value. A wrong value, such as `abc` or an interval of 0, stops the indexer at start.

# Which entry in packages/chains/src/chains.json to index. Defaults to robinhood-testnet.
# DROPCHAD_CHAIN=robinhood-testnet

# Blocks behind the head before a row is promoted from `seen` to `final`. Default 64.
# THIS IS A PLACEHOLDER. decides the real value. Robinhood Chain is an
# Arbitrum Orbit L2: the sequencer gives soft finality in seconds, but hard finality only comes
# when the batch is posted to Ethereum L1, which is far longer than 64 L2 blocks.
# CONFIRMATION_DEPTH=64

# How often the promotion job runs, in blocks. Default 200.
# FINALITY_CHECK_INTERVAL=200

# The anvil check only, never on the server. A local chain file in the
# registry shape with one entry, chain id 31337, used instead of DROPCHAD_CHAIN. The indexer
# refuses it when NODE_ENV is production. src/local-chain.ts.
# INDEXER_LOCAL_CHAIN=
